<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Loango Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Loango Bay is a bay on the Atlantic coast of the present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-the-congo">Republic of the Congo</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pointe-noire">Pointe-Noire</a>. It was the main harbour of the Kingdom of Loango, whose capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-loango">Mbanza Loango</a> (Buali) lay nearby. From the 17th century European traders came to it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raffia-cloth">raffia cloth</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, and in the 18th century it became one of the busiest slave-trading ports of the Loango coast.</p></div>
